Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/view/Choreographer.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0),
ADR-0041 a): setFPSDivisor keeps the divisor but tells no ThreadedRenderer.

Why: every Choreographer's constructor calls setFPSDivisor, which hands the divisor on to hwui's render thread through
ThreadedRenderer, a static method of HardwareRenderer, the GPU pipeline. Minato's views draw in software (ADR-0043
decision 2), so framework.jar leaves HardwareRenderer and ThreadedRenderer out, and the call would end the app with
NoClassDefFoundError. Without a render thread there is nothing to tell; Choreographer's own frame skipping by the
divisor stays as it is.

--- a/core/java/android/view/Choreographer.java
+++ b/core/java/android/view/Choreographer.java
@@ -835,7 +835,6 @@
     void setFPSDivisor(int divisor) {
         if (divisor <= 0) divisor = 1;
         mFPSDivisor = divisor;
-        ThreadedRenderer.setFPSDivisor(divisor);
     }
 
     private void traceMessage(String msg) {
